{"name":"Biology Experiments","hex":"#91a135","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"biology","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The study of all life or living matter.","The living organisms of a particular region."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biology"},{"term":"experiments","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of experiment"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of experiment"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experiments"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biology","blocks":[{"text":"Biology is the scientific study of life and living organisms. It is a broad natural science that encompasses a wide range of fields and unifying principles that explain the structure, function, growth, origin, evolution, and distribution of life. Central to biology are five fundamental themes: the cell as the basic unit of life, genes and heredity as the basis of inheritance, evolution as the driver of biological diversity, energy transformation for sustaining life processes, and homeostasis, the maintenance of internal stability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/DNA_simple_horizontal.svg/330px-DNA_simple_horizontal.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biology","wikidata":"Q420"},{"title":"Experiment","blocks":[{"text":"An experiment is a procedure carried out to support or refute a hypothesis, or determine the efficacy or likelihood of something previously untried. Experiments provide insight into cause-and-effect by demonstrating what outcome occurs when a particular factor is manipulated. Experiments vary greatly in goal and scale but always rely on repeatable procedure and logical analysis of the results. There also exist natural experimental studies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Apollo_15_feather_and_hammer_drop.ogv/330px--Apollo_15_feather_and_hammer_drop.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Experiment","wikidata":"Q101965"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Charles_Darwin_aged_51.jpg/330px-Charles_Darwin_aged_51.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Charles_Darwin_aged_51.jpg/330px-Charles_Darwin_aged_51.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In 1842, Charles Darwin penned his first sketch of On the Origin of Species.[20]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Darwin_aged_51.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Mirror_baby.jpg/500px-Mirror_baby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Mirror_baby.jpg/500px-Mirror_baby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Even very young children perform rudimentary experiments to learn about the world and how things work.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMirror_baby.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Humanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG/500px-Humanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Humanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG/1280px-Humanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Humanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG/500px-Humanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumanit%C3%A9s_Num%C3%A9riques.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com